@startuml
title CycleFar — Create a training plan

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "TrainingPlansController" as Controller
collections "Owner-bound\nRails session draft" as Draft
control "PlanConfiguration" as Configuration
control "PlanBuilder" as Builder
control "Workout engine" as Engine
control "WeeklyLoadCap +\nLoadReduction" as LoadRules
control "PreviewPresenter" as Presenter
control "PlanCreator" as Creator
control "HorizonMaterializer" as Materializer
database "PostgreSQL" as Database

== Preview: no plan records are written ==
Rider -> Controller: POST preview with configuration
Controller -> Configuration: normalize and validate inputs
alt invalid configuration
  Controller --> Rider: 422 with form errors
else valid configuration
  Controller -> Draft: save inputs with Current.user.id
  Controller --> Rider: redirect to GET preview
  Rider -> Controller: GET preview
  Controller -> Draft: read draft for Current.user
  alt missing or different owner
    Controller -> Draft: clear stale/foreign draft if present
    Controller --> Rider: redirect to plan form
  else owned draft
    Controller -> Configuration: validate restored inputs
    alt restored inputs invalid
      Controller -> Draft: clear invalid draft
      Controller --> Rider: redirect to plan form
    else valid inputs
      Controller -> Builder: preview(configuration)
      Builder -> Builder: allocate phases, recovery, taper and FTP tests
      Builder -> Engine: forecast workouts with explicit variations and metrics
      Builder -> LoadRules: enforce ordered reductions on comparable hard weeks
      LoadRules --> Builder: adjusted definitions, metrics and infeasible warnings
      Builder --> Controller: in-memory preview
      Controller -> Presenter: format preview
      Controller --> Rider: show review screen
    end
  end
end

== Confirmation: create plan and near-term detail ==
Rider -> Controller: POST create plan
Controller -> Draft: read and consume owner-bound draft
Controller -> Configuration: validate restored inputs
alt missing or invalid draft
  Controller --> Rider: redirect to plan form
else valid draft
  Controller -> Creator: create!(configuration, Current.user)
  Creator -> Builder: rebuild deterministic preview
  Builder -> LoadRules: enforce ordered forecast load cap
  Builder --> Creator: phases, outlines, forecasts and generation choices
  group database transaction
    Creator -> Database: create owned plan, phases, template, event and outlines\npersist subtype, variation, ceilings and target/filler choices
    Creator -> Materializer: structure today..day 13 outlines
    Materializer -> Database: lock plan; read eligible outlines and fixed weekly load
    Materializer -> Engine: apply accepted bias/ceilings; generate actual definitions\nsample initial endurance profile once
    Engine --> Materializer: canonical steps and current-FTP metrics
    Materializer -> LoadRules: recheck actual load against comparable hard weeks
    LoadRules --> Materializer: bounded definitions retaining sampled profiles and duration
    Materializer -> Database: save steps, profile, effective level and automatic load references
  end
  Creator --> Controller: created plan
  Controller --> Rider: redirect to training calendar
end

note over Builder, Database
  Forecasts use explicit variations; sampled endurance profiles are saved at materialisation.
  Reduction order: level, variation, work target, compatible broad subtype, easy filler.
  Normal duration and specific subtype intent remain fixed. If infeasible, warn.
  Partial, recovery, taper and assessment weeks are not hard-week baselines.
  HomeController later rolls the horizon and reviews load without regenerating fixed detail.
end note
@enduml
